      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand that scheduling and managing medical appointments can be frustrating. However, it's very risky to take Vitamin K and Warfarin without a prescription because their interactions aren't something that can be managed effectively through self-medication. Conveniently taking them on separate days isn't a guarantee that won't prevent potential issues. Your health is too important, and this could be a serious matter. To avoid complications, please review this matter with your healthcare team when you can, and they can help you find the safest way to supplement your Vitamin K intake.",
      "source": "target",
